==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 40~60 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Mr. Angel]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 33.33~46.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,400f</sup>.
*3 [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 0.67~2 seconds<sup>20f~60f</sup>.
*3 [[Mr. Angel]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 3.33~5.33 seconds<sup>100f~160f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Divine Cyclone]] spawns as the boss.
**5 [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.
**3 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn, delay 20~33.33 seconds<sup>600f~1,000f</sup>.
**5 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.
**3 [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 0.67 seconds<sup>20f</sup>.
**3 [[Mr. Angel]]s spawn, delay 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>.
**1 [[Angelic Sleipnir]] spawns.
**10 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
**1 [[Othom]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Treat this stage as [[Rutsborg Vortex]] but with the added Divine Cyclone. Use [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman]] because Othom's a Floating enemy and it can take 1 hit before getting [[Curse]]d again. Using Talented [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] is an option as well, but its range doesn't make it an ideal choice here. A Talented [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk]] is a solid choice for this stage, because of its range and slow uptime. An alternative strategy is to lure Othom, rush him with [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N]] and [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Elder Mask Doron]], and kill him before the Divine Cyclone even comes close.

